<https://github.com/tumelomodise/LFTDO#Location> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Locations are farmer area where the livestock are being kept is referred to as a Farm.It can be at an urban, rural, or semi-urban location, and may have pen and open fields that are fenced or unfenced. \n\nThe position of livestock within a farm location is constrained to date and time, and their behavior influences their movement. The livestock position within a location may be indicated with coordinates such as longitude and latitude, which are used to precisely determine the location of livestock within a farm area, as discussed by  (Symeonaki et al., 2020).\n\nRelationships:\n1.Location (e.g., a farm) has a specific time period(startTime and endTime) during which certain events or activities occurs.\n2.Location (e.g., a farm) has a specific geographical position defined by latitude and longitude coordinates." .
<https://github.com/tumelomodise/LFTDO#Location> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Location" .
